        "biography": "Yang Jin-mo\u00a0(Korean:\u00a0\uc591\uc9c4\ubaa8) is a South Korean film editor. He is best known internationally for his work on multiple\u00a0Academy Award\u00a0winner\u00a0Parasite's editor, which earned him critical appraisal and recognition, including an\u00a0American Cinema Editors Award for Best Edited Feature Film \u2013 Dramatic\u00a0at the\u00a0American Cinema Editors Awards\u00a0in 2020 and the 2019\u00a0Online Film Critics Society Award for Best Editing.\u00a0This made\u00a0Parasite\u00a0the first non-English-language film to win the top prize at the\u00a0American Cinema Editors' Eddie Awards.\u00a0He was also nominated for the\u00a0Academy Award for Best Editing\u00a0for his work on\u00a0Parasite.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia Yang Jin-mo, article licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.",
